  "verbalization": "Ofloxacin is implicated in the treatment of Urinary Tract Infection (UTI) through a chain of indications that connect it to other antibiotics, which in turn are linked to UTI. The evidence suggests that Ofloxacin may be repurposed for UTI due to its ability to target bacterial infections, as it is indicated for prostatitis and rhinoscleroma, both of which can lead to UTI through systemic or local infection pathways. The presence of multiple indirect pathways—each involving a different antibiotic—indicates that Ofloxacin may exert a broad antimicrobial effect, potentially making it a viable candidate for UTI treatment. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ofloxacin to be repurposed in the context of UTI, supported by its role in treating conditions that can predispose to UTI. The evidence underscores the importance of considering the broader pharmacological profile of antibiotics in the context of disease repurposing.",
